: overcoming the obstacles to a sustainable, affordable medicine</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>New Brunswick: Rutgers University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nava-Ocampo</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Alarcon-Almanza</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Moyao-Garc&#x000fd;a</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ram&#x000ed;rez-Mora</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Salmer&#x000f3;n</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Undocumented drug utilization and drug waste increase costs of pediatric anesthesia care</article-title><source>Fundam Clin Pharmacol</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14748762</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.0767-3981.2003.00214.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diehl</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Goo</surname><given-names>EDH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sumiye</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reducing waste of intravenous solutions</article-title><source>Am J Hosp Pharm</source><year>1992</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>106</fpage><lpage>108</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1570849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Favier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Fliche</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bressolle</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Economic benefit of a centralized reconstitution unit 